1
00:00:01,733 --> 00:00:03,693
They're about to exit the tunnel!

2
00:00:06,073 --> 00:00:08,733
No! Not good! Darby's ahead!

3
00:00:08,953 --> 00:00:10,553
And by a full car length!

4
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:12,710
Our speed is about to be doubled!

5
00:00:12,793 --> 00:00:14,233
It looks like I win!

6
00:00:16,053 --> 00:00:16,883
No!

7
00:00:16,966 --> 00:00:20,574
The fact of the matter is, I still
have more speed than you, Darby!

8
00:00:21,933 --> 00:00:23,333
You're in for it now!

9
00:00:27,493 --> 00:00:28,323
No!

10
00:00:28,406 --> 00:00:29,993
I can't believe what I'm seeing!

11
00:00:31,153 --> 00:00:33,350
Cocculeen had enough power
to spin his car around

12
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:36,139
and knock Darby's car
clear off the racetrack!

13
00:00:36,253 --> 00:00:38,893
He used his speed to
his advantage! Uh-huh!

14
00:00:39,473 --> 00:00:40,733
He's out of there!

15
00:00:42,313 --> 00:00:44,901
And Cocculeen's car is
safely on the ground!

16
00:00:45,153 --> 00:00:46,373
You did it!

17
00:00:46,993 --> 00:00:49,253
The weaker car loses in a collision.

18
00:00:49,673 --> 00:00:53,110
Giving up power to ram me will
prove to be a costly mistake.

19
00:00:53,193 --> 00:00:54,310
Instead of gloating,

20
00:00:54,393 --> 00:00:56,350
you should have paid more
attention to my plan to stay

21
00:00:56,433 --> 00:00:59,433
behind and knock you off
course with a spin attack.

22
00:00:59,793 --> 00:01:03,433
So you say though the same
could also be said of you?

23
00:01:04,333 --> 00:01:06,453
Losing power was not an accident.

24
00:01:07,053 --> 00:01:10,233
You're so self-righteous in your hubris.

25
00:01:10,393 --> 00:01:14,099
You didn't realize I planned for
you to knock my car off course

26
00:01:14,633 --> 00:01:16,613
Everything rests on this

27
00:01:17,273 --> 00:01:18,313
Look closely.

28
00:01:18,513 --> 00:01:20,513
Do you see where my car is headed?

29
00:01:30,373 --> 00:01:34,713
He landed on the other side,
farther ahead at that! Impossible!

30
00:01:36,033 --> 00:01:37,073
Yes, ordinarily.

31
00:01:37,473 --> 00:01:39,090
Even at one's top speed,

32
00:01:39,173 --> 00:01:42,770
a move like the one I just did
usually would result in a crash.

33
00:01:42,853 --> 00:01:45,670
You wouldn't make it by
jumping over the curves.

34
00:01:45,753 --> 00:01:49,577
But it's another story completely
if you're catapulted over them.

35
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:52,113
All I needed was your help.

36
00:01:52,953 --> 00:01:54,850
From the moment we left the tunnel,

37
00:01:54,933 --> 00:01:58,286
my plan was to get you to hit
me by sacrificing my power.

38
00:01:58,733 --> 00:02:03,813
That said, I think it's time we
continued our race, don't you?

39
00:02:05,033 --> 00:02:08,473
Don't let this guy get to
you, Kakyoin! Stay focused!

40
00:02:14,913 --> 00:02:15,743
Kakyoin!

41
00:02:15,973 --> 00:02:19,393
There, now his soul belongs to me.

42
00:02:19,873 --> 00:02:21,993
The poor fool admitted defeat.

43
00:02:22,693 --> 00:02:26,533
He finally realized that it was
pointless to continue racing.

44
00:02:29,013 --> 00:02:30,333
Still, I must say,

45
00:02:30,753 --> 00:02:34,988
you, Kakyoin, are the first opponent
to ever make me perspire like this.

46
00:02:41,273 --> 00:02:42,833
Given its source material,

47
00:02:43,113 --> 00:02:47,289
this doll will make a most exquisite
addition to my growing collection.

48
00:02:47,853 --> 00:02:51,030
He was the very first opponent
to muster up the courage to

49
00:02:51,113 --> 00:02:55,054
conquer his fears and resist cracking
under such colossal pressure.

50
00:03:02,533 --> 00:03:06,073
I will treasure his good company always.

51
00:03:08,593 --> 00:03:09,423
Careful,

52
00:03:09,506 --> 00:03:11,410
it would be in the best interest of all

53
00:03:11,493 --> 00:03:14,317
involved for you to keep
your emotions in check.

54
00:03:14,413 --> 00:03:16,413
Harming me is out of the question.

55
00:03:16,633 --> 00:03:20,810
You see, dying is something I simply
can't do if you want your friend back.

56
00:03:20,893 --> 00:03:23,270
Slipping on a banana
peel and hitting my head.

57
00:03:23,353 --> 00:03:24,693
choking on gum,

58
00:03:24,893 --> 00:03:28,950
or even suffering a heart attack from
the shock of popping a bag of popcorn.

59
00:03:29,033 --> 00:03:33,853
If any of those things sent me to
heaven, Kakyoin's soul would go too.

60
00:03:57,753 --> 00:04:00,353
That's it.

61
00:04:23,353 --> 00:04:24,473
Good to know.

62
00:04:26,893 --> 00:04:29,730
The end of the story. When I was born.

63
00:04:29,813 --> 00:04:31,490
I was born in a moment.

64
00:04:31,573 --> 00:04:34,010
I'm going to walk.

65
00:04:34,093 --> 00:04:34,950
I'm going to walk.

66
00:04:35,033 --> 00:04:38,770
Good to see you now.

67
00:04:38,853 --> 00:04:40,990
The last page. That's the last page.

68
00:04:41,073 --> 00:04:42,150
The last page.

69
00:04:42,233 --> 00:04:43,770
That's the last page.

70
00:04:43,853 --> 00:04:48,113
End of the world.

71
00:04:53,553 --> 00:04:55,133
Oh. Oh. Oh. Oh.

72
00:05:18,773 --> 00:05:19,603
What the?

73
00:05:19,733 --> 00:05:22,113
Hey, Jotaro, wait! What's this?

74
00:05:22,513 --> 00:05:23,533
Hey, Jotaro!

75
00:05:23,813 --> 00:05:25,330
Why the hell are you sitting down?

76
00:05:25,413 --> 00:05:27,350
We should be kicking Geppetto's ass!

77
00:05:27,433 --> 00:05:28,633
I'll play him next!

78
00:05:28,933 --> 00:05:32,345
Old man, have you ever actually
played any of these games?

79
00:05:32,573 --> 00:05:35,102
If not, the odds wouldn't
be in your favor.

80
00:05:37,873 --> 00:05:39,473
Stay out of it, old man.

81
00:05:39,753 --> 00:05:42,871
This isn't your average game
of gin rummy, after all.

82
00:05:44,813 --> 00:05:46,273
We're playing baseball.

83
00:05:46,953 --> 00:05:50,473
That's the game I choose to
settle this once and for all.

84
00:05:52,453 --> 00:05:54,693
As collateral, I'll bet my soul.

85
00:05:55,713 --> 00:05:58,595
Alright, then I would like
to bet Kakyoin's soul.

86
00:06:00,813 --> 00:06:03,453
My stand, Atum, has released your arm.

87
00:06:03,633 --> 00:06:05,574
You may thank me at your leisure.

88
00:06:05,993 --> 00:06:08,581
Now that Kakyoin's soul
is in my collection,

89
00:06:08,893 --> 00:06:13,010
there's no longer reason for me to
keep your arm in my stand's clutches.

90
00:06:13,093 --> 00:06:14,393
And suffice it to say,

91
00:06:14,653 --> 00:06:19,013
I'd be at a bit of a disadvantage if
I faced you with my stand one-handed.

92
00:06:19,393 --> 00:06:23,452
I'm all aware of your Star Platinum's
incredible speed and precision.

93
00:06:25,413 --> 00:06:28,790
Really, out of all the games
you could have chosen to play,

94
00:06:28,873 --> 00:06:33,433
it's unfortunate for you that
we're playing my specialty.

95
00:06:34,093 --> 00:06:34,923
Darby,

96
00:06:35,073 --> 00:06:38,210
just you wait the moment Jotaro
wipes the floor with you,

97
00:06:38,293 --> 00:06:40,470
I'll throttle the life
out of your pompous ass.

98
00:06:40,553 --> 00:06:41,847
And that is a promise!

99
00:06:47,033 --> 00:06:49,133
Oh, that's a baseball!

100
00:06:52,833 --> 00:06:55,410
Doesn't look like he's
tempered with this game either.

101
00:06:55,493 --> 00:06:56,552
You're good to go.

102
00:06:57,573 --> 00:07:00,338
Before we begin, you'll
need to pick your team.

103
00:07:03,433 --> 00:07:04,263
Jaguars.

104
00:07:05,033 --> 00:07:05,863
Jaguars!

105
00:07:06,793 --> 00:07:08,053
Yes, I see.

106
00:07:08,413 --> 00:07:11,670
You've decided to go with a team
that is a strong offense, eh?

107
00:07:11,753 --> 00:07:14,253
and two with a batting average over 400.

108
00:07:14,733 --> 00:07:18,110
If that's how you're going to play
it, I'll choose the Red Dragons.

109
00:07:18,193 --> 00:07:19,193
Red Dragons!

110
00:07:20,893 --> 00:07:22,011
Offense or defense?

111
00:07:22,373 --> 00:07:23,693
Go on, take your pick.

112
00:07:25,393 --> 00:07:26,223
Offense.

113
00:07:26,306 --> 00:07:29,493
In that case, the Jaguars will bat first.

114
00:07:30,673 --> 00:07:35,614
Next, you can begin designing your own
players by drawing their faces on the screen.

115
00:07:36,353 --> 00:07:39,373
This handsome devil is Star Platinum.

116
00:07:41,033 --> 00:07:44,750
Now that we've gotten the
preparations out of the way...

117
00:07:44,833 --> 00:07:45,773
Playball!

118
00:07:48,933 --> 00:07:51,333
Jaguars versus Red Dragon!

119
00:07:52,493 --> 00:07:53,323
Playball!

120
00:08:01,033 --> 00:08:03,753
I've chosen number 15 as my pitcher.

121
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:06,409
January 5th is my birthday, you know.

122
00:08:09,753 --> 00:08:11,313
Now, here we go.

123
00:08:11,673 --> 00:08:13,373
The pitcher is winding up!

124
00:08:15,373 --> 00:08:16,314
The first pitch!

125
00:08:18,133 --> 00:08:18,963
What?

126
00:08:21,133 --> 00:08:21,993
Strike one!

127
00:08:23,033 --> 00:08:26,053
Uh, hey, I don't get it. What's wrong?

128
00:08:26,313 --> 00:08:28,310
That was a pretty amateur move back there.

129
00:08:28,393 --> 00:08:33,334
It's great that you swung the bat and all,
but it was before he even threw the ball!

130
00:08:39,533 --> 00:08:40,363
Hey!

131
00:08:40,453 --> 00:08:41,747
What's this all about?

132
00:08:42,033 --> 00:08:45,050
There's no need for you to
practice your swing, is there?

133
00:08:45,133 --> 00:08:45,993
Hang on!

134
00:08:46,333 --> 00:08:47,650
Jotaro, is this...

135
00:08:47,733 --> 00:08:50,633
the very first time
you've ever played this?

136
00:08:50,933 --> 00:08:54,227
In fact, have you ever played
a video game in your life?

137
00:08:55,093 --> 00:08:58,433
You answer me right now, Jotaro! Relax.

138
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:01,031
I already know how to play baseball.

139
00:09:01,273 --> 00:09:03,744
I'll figure out the game controls as I go.

140
00:09:04,713 --> 00:09:06,810
What are you saying?!

141
00:09:06,893 --> 00:09:10,090
In case you haven't noticed,
your timing is totally off!

142
00:09:10,173 --> 00:09:11,733
Your swings are pathetic!

143
00:09:12,153 --> 00:09:15,271
Don't lie, this is your
first time playing, isn't it?

144
00:09:24,533 --> 00:09:25,393
Strike two!

145
00:09:27,073 --> 00:09:30,970
And now you're actually swinging the bat
after the catcher has caught the ball!

146
00:09:31,053 --> 00:09:32,750
You don't know what you're doing!

147
00:09:32,833 --> 00:09:34,270
Damn it, Jotaro, I was right!

148
00:09:34,353 --> 00:09:37,529
You don't know a video game
from a hole in the ground!

149
00:09:37,693 --> 00:09:39,013
Strike! Better out!

150
00:09:40,773 --> 00:09:42,690
Jotaro, it's time to get serious!

151
00:09:42,773 --> 00:09:45,170
Stop trying to act cool
and use your blasted head!

152
00:09:45,253 --> 00:09:46,710
You bet your soul on this game,

153
00:09:46,793 --> 00:09:49,390
so if you think you can back
out due to lack of experience,

154
00:09:49,473 --> 00:09:51,033
think again! Good grief.

155
00:09:51,393 --> 00:09:53,922
This is the worst pep
talk I've ever heard.

156
00:09:54,033 --> 00:09:55,690
You should be more encouraging.

157
00:09:55,773 --> 00:09:59,210
Try something like, it's only the first
inning, you can still make a comeback.

158
00:09:59,293 --> 00:10:01,030
What the hell's going
through that head of yours?

159
00:10:01,113 --> 00:10:05,570
You can't possibly rely solely on Star
Platinum's reflexes to win this game,

160
00:10:05,653 --> 00:10:06,483
can you?

161
00:10:06,566 --> 00:10:07,396
Think about it!

162
00:10:07,479 --> 00:10:09,170
You don't know the first
thing about video games!

163
00:10:09,253 --> 00:10:11,194
How are you supposed to beat him?

164
00:10:11,833 --> 00:10:13,304
What's your plan, Jotaro?

165
00:10:13,633 --> 00:10:14,753
Answer me, dammit!

166
00:10:14,973 --> 00:10:17,620
Do you have a way to
beat this weirdo or not?

167
00:10:19,153 --> 00:10:19,983
Jotaro?

168
00:10:21,373 --> 00:10:22,203
Listen,

169
00:10:22,286 --> 00:10:25,330
if your strategy is to trick me
by pretending to be an amateur,

170
00:10:25,413 --> 00:10:28,119
let me inform you that
it isn't going to work.

171
00:10:28,873 --> 00:10:31,755
I'd never be foolish enough
to let my guard down.

172
00:10:32,013 --> 00:10:34,670
Even if you were a helpless
child, it wouldn't happen.

173
00:10:34,753 --> 00:10:36,333
A soul is at stake.

174
00:10:38,233 --> 00:10:42,233
Old man, since you wanted to
know, I don't have a plan.

175
00:10:43,033 --> 00:10:43,863
However,

176
00:10:44,013 --> 00:10:45,413
if I did have one,

177
00:10:45,813 --> 00:10:47,770
the only thing it would
involve would be knocking

178
00:10:47,853 --> 00:10:50,290
the nose straight off the
face of this condescending,

179
00:10:50,373 --> 00:10:53,902
overinflated douchebag of a
prick taking up space beside me.

180
00:10:54,213 --> 00:10:57,037
All I care about is getting
Kakyoin's soul back.

181
00:10:57,213 --> 00:10:58,833
I'll do whatever it takes.

182
00:11:00,953 --> 00:11:02,493
You talk a big game,

183
00:11:02,633 --> 00:11:05,670
but it's still the top of the
first inning and you have won out.

184
00:11:05,753 --> 00:11:07,341
The match is far from over.

185
00:11:07,613 --> 00:11:09,590
And since you haven't played before,

186
00:11:09,673 --> 00:11:12,630
you should know that if you
fall more than 11 points behind,

187
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:13,543
you lose.

188
00:11:18,233 --> 00:11:20,433
Second batter, number three!

189
00:11:24,673 --> 00:11:25,503
Strike!

190
00:11:25,993 --> 00:11:26,823
Damn!

191
00:11:26,906 --> 00:11:28,290
He's getting even worse!

192
00:11:28,373 --> 00:11:31,470
That time he swung the bat over
40 centimeters above the ball!

193
00:11:31,553 --> 00:11:32,494
How's he so bad?

194
00:11:33,273 --> 00:11:35,233
Strike two! What?

195
00:11:35,393 --> 00:11:36,628
It wasn't even close!

196
00:11:40,693 --> 00:11:42,833
Strike three! You're out!

197
00:11:45,433 --> 00:11:46,550
It's all over.

198
00:11:46,633 --> 00:11:49,045
Jotaro's no match for someone like Darby.

199
00:11:49,253 --> 00:11:53,250
This massacre is like being forced to watch
a group of high school baseball champs

200
00:11:53,333 --> 00:11:59,773
go head-to-head with kids from the knitting
club it's pathetic strike one strike two

201
00:12:02,413 --> 00:12:07,870
so it wasn't a bluff he really is a
beginner this is too easy in the same

202
00:12:07,953 --> 00:12:11,370
way a judo pro can gauge his opponent's
skill simply by looking at the

203
00:12:11,453 --> 00:12:16,210
way he wears his gi i can read him
like a book and chapter one is called

204
00:12:16,293 --> 00:12:22,513
jotaro the video game novice all the
same i refuse to let my guard down

205
00:12:23,613 --> 00:12:26,966
I'm aware of the weaknesses
of every batter in this game.

206
00:12:27,533 --> 00:12:29,886
Next will be a low pitch to the outside.

207
00:12:30,473 --> 00:12:34,993
I'll throw my best pitch, the
four-seam fastball, and strike him out.

208
00:12:35,433 --> 00:12:36,727
It's the first inning.

209
00:12:36,993 --> 00:12:39,273
Two outs, two strikes, and no fouls.

210
00:12:39,413 --> 00:12:41,893
Here comes my next pitch. Go right ahead.

211
00:12:42,453 --> 00:12:46,218
I've pretty much gotten the hang
of batting with the controller.

212
00:12:46,493 --> 00:12:48,213
Wait, what did he just say?

213
00:12:48,453 --> 00:12:50,100
I must have heard him wrong.

214
00:12:50,753 --> 00:12:51,893
What does he mean?

215
00:12:52,053 --> 00:12:53,171
Got the hang of it.

216
00:12:54,973 --> 00:12:56,653
Surely he couldn't have...

217
00:12:58,413 --> 00:12:59,953
What is he talking about?

218
00:13:00,253 --> 00:13:01,353
What does he mean?

219
00:13:07,553 --> 00:13:08,383
What?

220
00:13:08,873 --> 00:13:09,703
Jotaro!

221
00:13:10,173 --> 00:13:11,003
All right.

222
00:13:11,253 --> 00:13:13,330
I'm really starting to enjoy this game.

223
00:13:13,413 --> 00:13:14,243
What in the...

224
00:13:14,326 --> 00:13:16,413
It can't be! It's going!

225
00:13:16,773 --> 00:13:18,373
The ball is still going!

226
00:13:19,033 --> 00:13:20,621
It just doesn't make sense.

227
00:13:20,733 --> 00:13:23,027
What did he mean by got the hang of it?

228
00:13:23,453 --> 00:13:24,571
Got the hang of it?

229
00:13:24,933 --> 00:13:26,373
Got the hang of it?

230
00:13:29,793 --> 00:13:31,313
He did it!

231
00:13:31,533 --> 00:13:34,293
I don't know how, but he did it!

232
00:13:36,393 --> 00:13:37,593
Hey, Ron!

233
00:13:44,753 --> 00:13:45,733
Home run!

234
00:13:46,173 --> 00:13:47,533
It's a home run!

235
00:13:48,373 --> 00:13:49,733
Ha ha ha ha ha!

236
00:13:50,833 --> 00:13:52,573
Jotaro, damn you!

237
00:14:03,113 --> 00:14:05,553
Jotaro, did I really hear you correctly?

238
00:14:05,933 --> 00:14:06,833
Say something!

239
00:14:07,173 --> 00:14:10,330
It sounded like you've pretty
much gotten the hang of batting!

240
00:14:10,413 --> 00:14:12,472
I don't feel like repeating myself.

241
00:14:14,753 --> 00:14:17,953
He was a beginner when we
started this game. And yet,

242
00:14:18,153 --> 00:14:22,741
he's claiming to have learned proper
swinging technique in only eight pitches.

243
00:14:22,853 --> 00:14:26,813
Jotaro Code has all the speed
and dexterity of Star Platinum.

244
00:14:27,433 --> 00:14:32,053
Now I know why Master Dio finds him to
be problematic and why my brother lost.

245
00:14:37,833 --> 00:14:38,663
Interesting.

246
00:14:38,933 --> 00:14:41,730
I couldn't have asked for
a more fitting opponent.

247
00:14:41,813 --> 00:14:44,633
But, as naturally gifted as you may be,

248
00:14:45,013 --> 00:14:49,425
you made a critical mistake by revealing
your talents so early in the game.

249
00:14:50,093 --> 00:14:52,593
A mistake that will cost you dearly.

250
00:14:55,593 --> 00:14:57,733
Let's resume the game, Jotaro.

251
00:15:02,993 --> 00:15:04,733
Yes, he did it!

252
00:15:05,213 --> 00:15:06,453
Bless, my boy!

253
00:15:06,893 --> 00:15:09,187
Another home run right out of the park!

254
00:15:10,033 --> 00:15:11,270
Talk about a comeback!

255
00:15:11,353 --> 00:15:12,970
Four runs in the first inning!

256
00:15:13,053 --> 00:15:16,053
Looks like you've got this
game in the bag, Jotaro!

257
00:15:16,193 --> 00:15:19,017
Keep it up, and we'll be
out of here in no time!

258
00:15:19,333 --> 00:15:20,193
Hey, Darby!

259
00:15:20,693 --> 00:15:24,752
You'll just ignore me, but I'll say
it anyway because I'm a nice guy!

260
00:15:25,113 --> 00:15:26,350
I'm giving you an out.

261
00:15:26,433 --> 00:15:31,010
All you have to do is return Kakyoin's soul
and take us to Dio of your own volition.

262
00:15:31,093 --> 00:15:33,564
If you cooperate, no harm will befall you.

263
00:15:40,453 --> 00:15:43,673
For all his faults, my
brother was a master gambler.

264
00:15:43,893 --> 00:15:46,246
He made conning people into an art form.

265
00:15:47,293 --> 00:15:50,590
You'd think his younger brother
would be perfect to practice on.

266
00:15:50,673 --> 00:15:51,933
But you'd be wrong.

267
00:15:52,213 --> 00:15:54,730
He never asked me to
play one game of poker.

268
00:15:54,813 --> 00:15:58,754
No, I was never asked to play any
games of the gambling persuasion.

269
00:15:58,933 --> 00:16:00,433
Any guesses why?

270
00:16:02,493 --> 00:16:03,733
When I was 15,

271
00:16:04,013 --> 00:16:07,450
I caught my brother putting his
oh-so-predictable moves on my girlfriend.

272
00:16:07,533 --> 00:16:11,093
He was 10 years older, but
I beat him to a bloody pulp.

273
00:16:11,413 --> 00:16:15,119
I broke his ribs and proceeded
to kick him until he spat blood.

274
00:16:15,413 --> 00:16:18,690
The last thing my brother said
to me was how sorry he was.

275
00:16:18,773 --> 00:16:20,313
Any idea why?

276
00:16:20,693 --> 00:16:23,993
Would you please cut to the
chase already? Even as kids,

277
00:16:24,213 --> 00:16:25,950
my brother had the good sense to realize

278
00:16:26,033 --> 00:16:28,470
that he'd never have
what it took to beat me.

279
00:16:28,553 --> 00:16:31,847
The reason for that is about
to become abundantly clear.

280
00:16:32,773 --> 00:16:37,893
At this moment, you have a false sense of
confidence due to the home run you hit.

281
00:16:38,193 --> 00:16:42,530
But deep down, you feel a sense of
unease, not unlike what my brother felt.

282
00:16:42,613 --> 00:16:45,378
My prowess is beginning
to worry you, isn't it?

283
00:16:45,593 --> 00:16:49,710
Right now, you're coming to a daunting
conclusion about the game's outcome,

284
00:16:49,793 --> 00:16:50,911
aren't you, Jotaro?

285
00:16:51,253 --> 00:16:53,371
What the hell are you talking about?

286
00:16:55,353 --> 00:16:56,412
Changing pictures!

287
00:16:56,793 --> 00:16:59,550
Number 15 is out and number 77 is in!

288
00:16:59,633 --> 00:17:05,313
77 is a power pitcher with a max pitch
speed of 165 kilometers per hour.

289
00:17:06,933 --> 00:17:09,345
Also, I'll tell you the pitch I'll throw.

290
00:17:10,593 --> 00:17:15,153
Number 77 will throw a forkball and
he'll throw it right down the middle.

291
00:17:16,213 --> 00:17:17,330
What the hell?

292
00:17:17,413 --> 00:17:19,350
Why would he declare what he's throwing?

293
00:17:19,433 --> 00:17:22,374
A forkball is about to
come barreling down center.

294
00:17:22,613 --> 00:17:24,437
But will you believe me or not?

295
00:17:24,753 --> 00:17:27,530
Jotaro, he's just spouting
nonsense to shake your confidence.

296
00:17:27,613 --> 00:17:30,593
Do yourself a favor and
ignore everything he says.

297
00:17:31,153 --> 00:17:32,633
Throw it, Darby.

298
00:17:33,573 --> 00:17:35,753
Will you believe or will you doubt?

299
00:17:41,773 --> 00:17:42,833
I knew it!

300
00:17:42,973 --> 00:17:45,470
It's a fastball, and
it's coming right at you!

301
00:17:45,553 --> 00:17:46,383
Let's see!

302
00:17:46,466 --> 00:17:48,250
Is the ball going to change direction?

303
00:17:48,333 --> 00:17:50,573
The suspense is driving me crazy!

304
00:17:52,013 --> 00:17:53,053
You swung!

305
00:17:53,293 --> 00:17:55,470
You bought his act and
bet on the forkball!

306
00:17:55,553 --> 00:17:56,833
It's still going.

307
00:17:57,093 --> 00:17:58,993
It actually is a fastball.

308
00:17:59,813 --> 00:18:00,873
Oh, great.

309
00:18:01,013 --> 00:18:02,778
He hit the bottom of the ball.

310
00:18:04,293 --> 00:18:05,123
Out!

311
00:18:05,713 --> 00:18:07,853
First inning, three outs change.

312
00:18:12,373 --> 00:18:13,913
Idiot, how could you?

313
00:18:14,253 --> 00:18:16,530
Leave it to a rookie
for something like that.

314
00:18:16,613 --> 00:18:19,025
I can't believe you swung for a forkball.

315
00:18:20,813 --> 00:18:21,643
No.

316
00:18:22,033 --> 00:18:22,863
No.

317
00:18:22,946 --> 00:18:26,230
He had already seen through me and knew
I would swing expecting a forkball,

318
00:18:26,313 --> 00:18:28,433
so we switched it up to a fastball.

319
00:18:29,333 --> 00:18:30,610
But he has a point, though.

320
00:18:30,693 --> 00:18:34,070
Something's been gnawing at me ever
since we stepped foot in this mansion.

321
00:18:34,153 --> 00:18:35,273
I'm not sure how,

322
00:18:35,533 --> 00:18:40,004
but he knew Star Platinum would throw
a right punch in our earlier skirmish.

323
00:18:41,193 --> 00:18:42,023
What?

324
00:18:42,106 --> 00:18:42,936
Impossible!

325
00:18:43,019 --> 00:18:44,330
Are you trying to tell me
that he can read your mind?

326
00:18:44,413 --> 00:18:46,884
No offense, Jotaro, but that's crazy talk!

327
00:18:48,253 --> 00:18:49,841
Oh, would you look at that?

328
00:18:49,953 --> 00:18:51,153
It's my turn at bat.

329
00:19:01,093 --> 00:19:02,933
This is going to be a home run.

330
00:19:03,673 --> 00:19:08,379
Keep your eye on the birdie as I'll be
hitting it into the left field bleachers.

331
00:19:09,653 --> 00:19:14,390
Old man, are you absolutely sure the game
and console haven't been tampered with?

332
00:19:14,473 --> 00:19:16,090
Yeah, I'm positive it's clean.

333
00:19:16,173 --> 00:19:17,333
And that's not all.

334
00:19:17,533 --> 00:19:20,533
I haven't seen him make a
single funny move either.

335
00:19:20,653 --> 00:19:23,170
Then his secret weapon has
to be that stand of his.

336
00:19:23,253 --> 00:19:25,130
His stand doesn't just take souls.

337
00:19:25,213 --> 00:19:27,095
It must have some other ability.

338
00:19:29,653 --> 00:19:31,006
This will be my target.

339
00:19:34,893 --> 00:19:36,952
Now I'll get to the bottom of this.

340
00:19:37,453 --> 00:19:38,913
Has he lost his mind?

341
00:19:39,093 --> 00:19:41,710
He's going to try to hit
the banner on purpose?

342
00:19:41,793 --> 00:19:44,264
And where might you be aiming now, Jotaro?

343
00:19:44,633 --> 00:19:45,773
An inside pitch?

344
00:19:46,213 --> 00:19:47,613
Will you throw it high?

345
00:19:47,913 --> 00:19:48,970
Or low, perhaps?

346
00:19:49,053 --> 00:19:52,493
Or maybe you're planning some
kind of underhanded trick.

347
00:19:55,173 --> 00:19:56,003
Well...

348
00:20:01,933 --> 00:20:02,763
What the?

349
00:20:03,013 --> 00:20:05,601
He pulled back with
Jotaro through the ball!

350
00:20:09,453 --> 00:20:10,283
He...

351
00:20:10,366 --> 00:20:11,196
predicted it!

352
00:20:11,653 --> 00:20:12,483
He...

353
00:20:12,566 --> 00:20:14,753
knew exactly what would happen! But how?

354
00:20:15,073 --> 00:20:19,110
There's no way he could have seen that
pitch coming unless he read Jotaro's mind.

355
00:20:19,193 --> 00:20:20,073
Home run!

356
00:20:23,833 --> 00:20:24,893
That's one run.

357
00:20:25,673 --> 00:20:26,853
Damn this bastard.

358
00:20:27,313 --> 00:20:29,870
We faced all kinds of
opponents on this journey,

359
00:20:29,953 --> 00:20:32,130
but never one who could read our minds.

360
00:20:32,213 --> 00:20:36,090
If he really can read minds, then it
doesn't matter how clever we think we are.

361
00:20:36,173 --> 00:20:38,702
We won't stand a
snowball's chance in hell.

362
00:20:39,213 --> 00:20:41,233
Jotaro, what are you going to do?

363
00:20:54,233 --> 00:21:01,213
why that damn the punks declaring another
home run let's see uh an outside pitch

364
00:21:02,213 --> 00:21:06,753
or maybe you're going to aim low or
something in the vein of a fastball

365
00:21:18,153 --> 00:21:19,273
Home run!

366
00:21:20,393 --> 00:21:21,653
Four to two.

367
00:21:23,913 --> 00:21:24,743
Damn!

368
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:27,870
A person's body language and
the surrounding environment go

369
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:30,930
a long way toward helping
predict an opponent's next move.

370
00:21:31,013 --> 00:21:33,248
But there's no way to do it perfectly.

371
00:21:33,453 --> 00:21:37,233
And yet his stand predicts
Jotaro's pitch with 100 % accuracy.

372
00:21:37,633 --> 00:21:39,633
And technically he's not cheating.

373
00:21:41,313 --> 00:21:42,553
Another home run!

374
00:21:42,813 --> 00:21:43,931
It's four to three!

375
00:21:44,513 --> 00:21:47,650
How are we supposed to stop
him from reading our minds?

376
00:21:47,733 --> 00:21:48,563
How?

377
00:21:52,213 --> 00:21:56,033
At this rate, I'll be in the lead
in no time. Now, what's next?

378
00:21:56,313 --> 00:22:00,293
An inside pitch, a fastball, a
high pitch, or maybe a curveball?

379
00:22:00,673 --> 00:22:01,967
What's up your sleeve?

380
00:22:04,673 --> 00:22:05,503
Huh?

381
00:22:06,393 --> 00:22:07,353
Your hat.

382
00:22:08,273 --> 00:22:09,153
You idiot.

383
00:22:09,473 --> 00:22:13,414
Do you honestly take me for a cheat
like my ne 'er-do-well brother?

384
00:22:13,573 --> 00:22:15,170
Jotaro, you've got it wrong.

385
00:22:15,253 --> 00:22:16,900
Hiding your face is useless.

386
00:22:16,993 --> 00:22:18,390
I don't know what he's doing,

387
00:22:18,473 --> 00:22:21,430
but he's not watching the reflection
of the screen in your eyes.

388
00:22:21,513 --> 00:22:23,730
I get that it's hard not to go there now,

389
00:22:23,813 --> 00:22:27,890
but there's no way he can see what you're
pressing or what pitch you're choosing.

390
00:22:27,973 --> 00:22:30,330
Trust me, I've been watching
him the entire time.

391
00:22:30,413 --> 00:22:32,350
That's not what's been going on here.

392
00:22:32,433 --> 00:22:34,670
I only took off my hat
because I'm sweating.

393
00:22:34,753 --> 00:22:35,873
No other reason.

394
00:22:36,253 --> 00:22:39,253
Could you throw your next
pitch sometime this year?

395
00:22:40,633 --> 00:22:47,150
But I'm not going to be sweating anymore
I'll tell you my next pitch I'm throwing

396
00:22:47,233 --> 00:22:52,930
a high outside fastball you're joking
dotero do you hear what you're saying

397
00:22:53,013 --> 00:22:59,010
right now of course I do finally starting
to lose your hearing old man obviously

398
00:22:59,093 --> 00:23:03,973
I just told him my next pitch a high
outside fastball That's how I'm gonna win.

399
00:23:09,033 --> 00:23:09,863
Jotaro?

400
00:23:13,533 --> 00:23:16,613
Will you believe me, or will you doubt me?

401
00:23:19,853 --> 00:23:21,677
You're not too bright, are you?

402
00:23:28,313 --> 00:23:30,470
Do you hear what you're saying right now?

403
00:23:30,553 --> 00:23:32,550
Obviously, I just told him my next pitch.

404
00:23:32,633 --> 00:23:33,463
What the hell?

405
00:23:33,546 --> 00:23:34,570
He's telling the truth!

406
00:23:34,653 --> 00:23:35,483
Yes.

407
00:23:35,566 --> 00:23:36,450
You tampered with the console!

408
00:23:36,533 --> 00:23:37,363
No!

409
00:23:37,446 --> 00:23:39,150
It must have something to
do with that hat of yours!

410
00:23:39,233 --> 00:23:42,880
This is just a dance of deception
where the loser cries first.
